1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:06,388
This video sends records with exceptions to a topic of their own,

2
00:00:06,388 --> 00:00:09,590
so a bad record never stops the good ones.

3
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:14,664
Where video 2 left off, tutorial-in is blocked by one bad record,

4
00:00:14,664 --> 00:00:17,390
saved as the sample held-record.

5
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:21,708
Make a topic for them: smeltr-tutorial-exceptions.

6
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:28,560
In smeltr, you're on the branch tutorial-exceptions, where you saved the held record.

7
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:31,430
Open the route, and add a destination.

8
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:36,930
A new Kafka destination, tutorial-exceptions, writes to that topic.

9
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:52,023
Its condition is the other half: smeltr.exception isn't null.

10
00:00:52,440 --> 00:00:54,988
Now every record goes somewhere.

11
00:00:54,988 --> 00:00:59,765
Clean ones to tutorial-out, the rest to tutorial-exceptions.

12
00:00:59,765 --> 00:01:00,390
Save.

13
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:03,334
Test it with the record that blocked the source.

14
00:01:03,334 --> 00:01:05,683
Route the held-record sample.

15
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:10,558
It goes to tutorial-exceptions.

16
00:01:10,558 --> 00:01:12,430
Nothing is unmatched.

17
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:15,484
Open it for review, and deploy it.

18
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:30,173
The source reads again.

19
00:01:30,173 --> 00:01:32,379
The issue is gone.

20
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:35,643
Read the exceptions topic.

21
00:01:35,643 --> 00:01:39,155
The held record is there, with its exception.

22
00:01:45,200 --> 00:01:49,742
And the clean record that waited behind it reached tutorial-out.

23
00:01:57,960 --> 00:01:59,739
Check on learning.

24
00:01:59,939 --> 00:02:05,207
What two conditions send every record somewhere, clean or not?

25
00:02:09,607 --> 00:02:16,173
smeltr.exception equals null, and smeltr.exception isn't null.

26
00:02:17,073 --> 00:02:18,198
That's the course.

27
00:02:18,198 --> 00:02:23,235
Your bad records now have a place to go, and your sources keep flowing.
